1
00:00:00,182 --> 00:00:03,183
There are only four ways to
lose points on SAT quadratics.

2
00:00:03,825 --> 00:00:06,861
You read the solutions off the
factors with the wrong sign.

3
00:00:07,289 --> 00:00:09,825
You pick a form that
hides what they asked for.

4
00:00:10,003 --> 00:00:12,733
You give the x of the vertex
when they asked for the maximum.

5
00:00:12,753 --> 00:00:15,182
And the fourth one looks completely right,

6
00:00:15,397 --> 00:00:17,182
which is why it's so hard to catch.

7
00:00:17,216 --> 00:00:19,037
The first three are quick to fix.

8
00:00:19,430 --> 00:00:25,160
The fourth is forgetting the a when
you use the sum and product of the

9
00:00:25,180 --> 00:00:26,180
solutions.

10
00:00:26,323 --> 00:00:28,644
That's question six, the hardest one.

11
00:00:28,965 --> 00:00:34,287
Stay for it, because the fractions
you get look like real answers.

12
00:00:34,321 --> 00:00:38,178
One idea runs through
all of it: one parabola,

13
00:00:38,499 --> 00:00:42,321
three forms, and each form
shows you something different.

14
00:00:42,964 --> 00:00:46,285
Six practice questions, each
one harder than the last.

15
00:00:46,392 --> 00:00:49,285
Keep score as you go, and
see if you can get all six.

16
00:00:49,317 --> 00:00:51,637
Here's one parabola, written three ways.

17
00:00:52,138 --> 00:00:57,280
Standard form: y equals x
squared minus six x plus eight.

18
00:00:57,923 --> 00:01:02,031
Factored form: y equals x
minus two, times x minus four.

19
00:01:02,674 --> 00:01:05,333
Vertex form: y equals
x minus three, squared,

20
00:01:05,353 --> 00:01:06,368
minus one.

21
00:01:06,388 --> 00:01:08,210
All three make the same graph.

22
00:01:08,287 --> 00:01:10,715
Standard form shows the y intercept.

23
00:01:10,857 --> 00:01:15,394
It's the constant at the end, so this
parabola crosses the y axis at eight.

24
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,230
The leading coefficient
shows the direction.

25
00:01:18,250 --> 00:01:19,480
Positive opens up.

26
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:21,001
Negative opens down.

27
00:01:21,048 --> 00:01:22,992
Factored form shows the x intercepts,

28
00:01:23,012 --> 00:01:25,548
also called the zeros,
roots, or solutions.

29
00:01:26,012 --> 00:01:27,976
Set each factor equal to zero.

30
00:01:28,404 --> 00:01:32,405
x minus two gives two, and
x minus four gives four.

31
00:01:32,976 --> 00:01:34,119
Watch the sign.

32
00:01:34,191 --> 00:01:37,476
The factor says minus two,
but the root is positive two.

33
00:01:37,537 --> 00:01:39,966
Vertex form shows the vertex.

34
00:01:40,893 --> 00:01:44,910
x minus three, squared, minus
one puts the vertex at three,

35
00:01:44,930 --> 00:01:46,287
negative one.

36
00:01:46,822 --> 00:01:51,073
The x part flips sign again, but
the constant at the end doesn't.

37
00:01:51,573 --> 00:01:56,144
Since this parabola opens up,
negative one is its minimum value.

38
00:01:56,194 --> 00:01:58,051
Two more facts connect the forms.

39
00:01:58,193 --> 00:02:01,959
From standard form, the x coordinate
of the vertex is negative b over two a.

40
00:02:01,979 --> 00:02:05,530
Here, that's six over two, which is three.

41
00:02:05,550 --> 00:02:08,958
And the vertex always sits exactly
halfway between the two roots.

42
00:02:08,978 --> 00:02:11,015
Halfway between two and four is three.

43
00:02:11,059 --> 00:02:14,916
The SAT tests quadratics
in a few predictable ways.

44
00:02:15,273 --> 00:02:16,773
Solve the equation.

45
00:02:17,131 --> 00:02:19,523
Pick the form that shows a feature.

46
00:02:19,702 --> 00:02:22,131
Decide how many solutions there are.

47
00:02:22,309 --> 00:02:25,539
Find a maximum or minimum
in a word problem.

48
00:02:25,559 --> 00:02:28,631
And use the sum or
product of the solutions.

49
00:02:28,694 --> 00:02:32,066
The key on every one: before
you calculate anything,

50
00:02:32,086 --> 00:02:35,837
ask which form, or which formula,
gives you the answer for free.

51
00:02:35,864 --> 00:02:36,864
Question one.

52
00:02:37,042 --> 00:02:40,808
What are the solutions to the equation
x squared minus two x minus fifteen

53
00:02:40,828 --> 00:02:41,767
equals zero?

54
00:02:41,787 --> 00:02:42,894
Pause and try it.

55
00:02:46,103 --> 00:02:50,476
To factor, find two numbers that
multiply to negative fifteen and add to

56
00:02:50,496 --> 00:02:51,603
negative two.

57
00:02:52,210 --> 00:02:54,175
Negative five and three work.

58
00:02:54,675 --> 00:02:57,869
Negative five times three
is negative fifteen,

59
00:02:57,889 --> 00:03:00,496
and negative five plus
three is negative two.

60
00:03:00,555 --> 00:03:03,250
So the equation becomes x minus five,

61
00:03:03,270 --> 00:03:06,520
times x plus three, equals zero.

62
00:03:07,055 --> 00:03:08,607
Set each factor to zero.

63
00:03:08,627 --> 00:03:11,357
x equals five, or x equals negative three.

64
00:03:11,377 --> 00:03:12,805
The answer is B.

65
00:03:12,860 --> 00:03:14,646
A is the sign trap.

66
00:03:15,110 --> 00:03:18,162
Negative five and three are
the numbers inside the factors,

67
00:03:18,182 --> 00:03:19,503
not the solutions.

68
00:03:20,074 --> 00:03:22,967
If you're ever unsure, plug one back in.

69
00:03:23,645 --> 00:03:27,912
Negative five gives twenty-five
plus ten minus fifteen,

70
00:03:27,932 --> 00:03:29,753
which is twenty, not zero.

71
00:03:29,793 --> 00:03:30,829
Question two.

72
00:03:31,150 --> 00:03:35,166
The function f is defined by f of x
equals x squared plus four x minus

73
00:03:35,186 --> 00:03:36,186
twenty-one.

74
00:03:36,543 --> 00:03:40,486
Which of the following equivalent forms
of f of x displays the minimum value of

75
00:03:40,506 --> 00:03:42,471
f as a constant or coefficient?

76
00:03:42,559 --> 00:03:43,666
Pause and try it.

77
00:03:46,876 --> 00:03:49,876
Minimum value means the y
coordinate of the vertex.

78
00:03:50,232 --> 00:03:53,213
The form that shows the
vertex is vertex form:

79
00:03:53,233 --> 00:03:55,820
something squared, plus
or minus a constant,

80
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:57,483
with nothing else attached.

81
00:03:58,018 --> 00:03:59,018
That's C.

82
00:03:59,661 --> 00:04:02,642
x plus two, squared, minus twenty-five.

83
00:04:02,662 --> 00:04:05,483
The minimum value is negative twenty-five.

84
00:04:06,197 --> 00:04:08,640
A is factored form, so it shows the zeros,

85
00:04:08,660 --> 00:04:10,161
three and negative seven.

86
00:04:10,447 --> 00:04:12,927
B shows the y intercept,
negative twenty-one.

87
00:04:12,947 --> 00:04:13,604
And D is the trap.

88
00:04:13,624 --> 00:04:21,391
It has a squared term, but the extra ten
times the quantity x minus three means

89
00:04:21,411 --> 00:04:22,804
it isn't vertex form.

90
00:04:22,855 --> 00:04:27,085
To double check in Desmos, graph y
equals x squared plus four x minus

91
00:04:27,105 --> 00:04:31,283
twenty-one, zoom out, and
click the bottom of the curve.

92
00:04:31,427 --> 00:04:34,033
It shows negative two,
negative twenty-five.

93
00:04:34,094 --> 00:04:36,502
When a quadratic won't factor nicely,

94
00:04:36,522 --> 00:04:38,094
use the quadratic formula.

95
00:04:38,987 --> 00:04:44,074
x equals negative b, plus or minus the
square root of b squared minus four a c,

96
00:04:44,094 --> 00:04:45,272
all over two a.

97
00:04:45,766 --> 00:04:47,051
Question three.

98
00:04:47,444 --> 00:04:51,337
What are the solutions to two x squared
minus six x plus three equals zero?

99
00:04:51,359 --> 00:04:52,466
Pause and try it.

100
00:04:56,675 --> 00:05:01,640
Here a is two, b is negative
six, and c is three.

101
00:05:02,068 --> 00:05:03,925
Start with the part under the square root.

102
00:05:04,211 --> 00:05:07,120
b squared minus four a c is
thirty-six minus twenty-four,

103
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:08,210
which is twelve.

104
00:05:08,257 --> 00:05:11,665
So x equals six, plus or minus
the square root of twelve,

105
00:05:11,685 --> 00:05:12,737
all over four.

106
00:05:12,757 --> 00:05:15,486
The square root of
twelve is two root three.

107
00:05:15,506 --> 00:05:19,307
Divide every term by two, and you
get three plus or minus root three,

108
00:05:19,327 --> 00:05:20,380
all over two.

109
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:21,685
The answer is B.

110
00:05:21,762 --> 00:05:25,992
C is what you get if you
divide by two instead of two a.

111
00:05:26,012 --> 00:05:29,190
D comes from adding four a
c instead of subtracting it.

112
00:05:29,655 --> 00:05:32,655
And A uses b instead of negative b.

113
00:05:33,155 --> 00:05:35,869
Here, negative b is positive six.

114
00:05:35,933 --> 00:05:37,326
Desmos check.

115
00:05:37,647 --> 00:05:41,020
Graph y equals two x squared
minus six x plus three,

116
00:05:41,040 --> 00:05:42,861
and click the x intercepts.

117
00:05:43,289 --> 00:05:47,897
You get about zero point six three
four and two point three six six.

118
00:05:48,147 --> 00:05:50,627
Then type three plus
root three, all over two,

119
00:05:50,647 --> 00:05:52,111
on its own line.

120
00:05:52,826 --> 00:05:55,127
Desmos shows two point three six six.

121
00:05:55,147 --> 00:05:56,237
It matches.

122
00:05:56,257 --> 00:05:59,094
The part under the square
root, b squared minus four a c,

123
00:05:59,114 --> 00:06:00,523
is called the discriminant.

124
00:06:00,543 --> 00:06:04,059
It tells you how many real
solutions there are without solving.

125
00:06:04,079 --> 00:06:05,416
Positive means two.

126
00:06:05,436 --> 00:06:07,201
Zero means exactly one.

127
00:06:07,221 --> 00:06:08,613
Negative means none.

128
00:06:08,653 --> 00:06:13,403
On a graph, that's how many times
the parabola meets the x axis.

129
00:06:13,546 --> 00:06:16,526
It crosses twice, touches
once at the vertex,

130
00:06:16,546 --> 00:06:17,843
or never reaches it.

131
00:06:17,863 --> 00:06:19,149
Question four.

132
00:06:19,327 --> 00:06:23,486
In the equation nine x squared
minus twelve x plus c equals zero,

133
00:06:23,506 --> 00:06:24,863
c is a constant.

134
00:06:24,899 --> 00:06:27,629
If the equation has
exactly one real solution,

135
00:06:27,649 --> 00:06:29,149
what is the value of c?

136
00:06:29,247 --> 00:06:30,354
Pause and try it.

137
00:06:33,564 --> 00:06:37,170
Exactly one solution means
the discriminant equals zero.

138
00:06:38,064 --> 00:06:40,079
b squared is negative twelve squared,

139
00:06:40,099 --> 00:06:41,186
which is one hundred forty-four.

140
00:06:41,206 --> 00:06:47,671
Four a c is four times nine
times c, or thirty-six c.

141
00:06:48,349 --> 00:06:51,651
So one hundred forty-four
minus thirty-six c equals zero,

142
00:06:51,671 --> 00:06:53,135
and c equals four.

143
00:06:53,192 --> 00:06:54,192
Check it.

144
00:06:54,263 --> 00:06:58,636
Nine x squared minus twelve x
plus four is three x minus two,

145
00:06:58,656 --> 00:07:01,442
squared, a perfect
square with one solution.

146
00:07:01,692 --> 00:07:06,585
In Desmos, graph y equals nine
x squared minus twelve x plus c,

147
00:07:06,835 --> 00:07:11,192
add a slider for c, and drag until
the parabola just touches the x axis.

148
00:07:11,219 --> 00:07:12,969
That happens at c equals four.

149
00:07:13,016 --> 00:07:14,337
Question five.

150
00:07:14,765 --> 00:07:18,802
A company models its daily
profit P, in dollars,

151
00:07:18,944 --> 00:07:22,924
from selling a product at a price of p
dollars with the function P of p equals

152
00:07:22,944 --> 00:07:25,852
negative five p squared,
plus two hundred p,

153
00:07:25,872 --> 00:07:27,335
minus one thousand two hundred.

154
00:07:27,355 --> 00:07:30,691
According to the model, what
is the maximum daily profit,

155
00:07:30,711 --> 00:07:31,784
in dollars?

156
00:07:31,829 --> 00:07:32,936
Pause and try it.

157
00:07:37,146 --> 00:07:40,733
The leading coefficient is negative,
so the parabola opens down,

158
00:07:40,753 --> 00:07:42,753
and the vertex is the maximum.

159
00:07:43,217 --> 00:07:47,539
The p coordinate of the vertex
is negative b over two a.

160
00:07:48,288 --> 00:07:51,054
That's negative two
hundred over negative ten,

161
00:07:51,074 --> 00:07:52,289
which is twenty.

162
00:07:52,610 --> 00:07:54,425
Twenty dollars is the best price.

163
00:07:54,445 --> 00:07:57,353
But they asked for the profit.

164
00:07:57,373 --> 00:07:58,373
Plug in twenty.

165
00:07:58,552 --> 00:08:01,445
Negative five times four hundred
is negative two thousand.

166
00:08:02,516 --> 00:08:04,730
Two hundred times twenty is four thousand.

167
00:08:05,623 --> 00:08:07,888
Negative two thousand, plus four thousand,

168
00:08:07,908 --> 00:08:10,659
minus one thousand two
hundred, is eight hundred.

169
00:08:11,231 --> 00:08:13,909
The answer is B.

170
00:08:13,978 --> 00:08:15,621
Twenty is the trap.

171
00:08:15,764 --> 00:08:17,548
It's the price, not the profit.

172
00:08:18,264 --> 00:08:21,014
Two thousand eight hundred
drops the squared term.

173
00:08:21,585 --> 00:08:24,191
Four thousand eight hundred
gets its sign wrong.

174
00:08:24,268 --> 00:08:27,482
In Desmos, type it with x instead of p,

175
00:08:27,768 --> 00:08:30,376
zoom out, and click the top of the curve.

176
00:08:30,554 --> 00:08:32,947
Desmos shows twenty, eight hundred.

177
00:08:33,339 --> 00:08:35,375
The second number is the profit.

178
00:08:35,456 --> 00:08:36,742
Last concept.

179
00:08:37,171 --> 00:08:41,151
For any quadratic, a x
squared plus b x plus c,

180
00:08:41,171 --> 00:08:43,849
the solutions add up to negative b over a,

181
00:08:44,063 --> 00:08:46,135
and they multiply to c over a.

182
00:08:47,277 --> 00:08:49,635
You don't have to find
the solutions to use this.

183
00:08:49,703 --> 00:08:50,846
Quick example.

184
00:08:51,096 --> 00:08:55,167
x squared minus seven x plus
ten has solutions two and five.

185
00:08:55,203 --> 00:08:57,917
They add to seven, which
is negative b over a.

186
00:08:58,489 --> 00:09:01,346
And they multiply to
ten, which is c over a.

187
00:09:01,398 --> 00:09:03,898
Question six, the hardest one.

188
00:09:04,648 --> 00:09:08,520
The solutions to the equation three x
squared plus b x plus c equals zero,

189
00:09:08,540 --> 00:09:12,220
where b and c are constants, are
four and negative two thirds.

190
00:09:12,469 --> 00:09:14,398
What is the value of b plus c?

191
00:09:14,485 --> 00:09:15,628
Pause and try it.

192
00:09:15,843 --> 00:09:17,521
Take a little longer on this one.

193
00:09:21,802 --> 00:09:22,944
Start with the sum.

194
00:09:23,551 --> 00:09:26,659
Four plus negative two
thirds is ten thirds.

195
00:09:26,873 --> 00:09:30,515
The sum is negative b
over a, and a is three.

196
00:09:30,872 --> 00:09:33,924
So negative b over
three equals ten thirds,

197
00:09:33,944 --> 00:09:35,766
and b equals negative ten.

198
00:09:35,818 --> 00:09:36,818
Now the product.

199
00:09:37,246 --> 00:09:40,353
Four times negative two thirds
is negative eight thirds.

200
00:09:41,032 --> 00:09:46,762
The product is c over a, so c over
three equals negative eight thirds,

201
00:09:46,782 --> 00:09:49,032
and c equals negative eight.

202
00:09:49,460 --> 00:09:53,369
So b plus c is negative
ten plus negative eight,

203
00:09:53,389 --> 00:09:54,853
which is negative eighteen.

204
00:09:54,907 --> 00:09:56,993
You can confirm it with factored form.

205
00:09:57,013 --> 00:10:00,050
A solution of four means
a factor of x minus four.

206
00:10:00,157 --> 00:10:03,814
A solution of negative two thirds
means a factor of three x plus two.

207
00:10:03,834 --> 00:10:08,763
Multiply them, and you get three
x squared minus ten x minus eight.

208
00:10:09,050 --> 00:10:11,085
Same b, same c.

209
00:10:11,109 --> 00:10:13,145
The trap is forgetting the a.

210
00:10:14,859 --> 00:10:19,822
If you treat the sum as just
negative b and the product as just c,

211
00:10:19,895 --> 00:10:23,787
you get fractions for b and
c, and the wrong answer.

212
00:10:23,836 --> 00:10:25,550
Here's the test-day checklist.

213
00:10:25,835 --> 00:10:29,995
First, read exactly what
they want: the solutions,

214
00:10:30,015 --> 00:10:33,066
the vertex, a maximum or minimum value,

215
00:10:33,086 --> 00:10:35,764
the number of solutions,
or a sum or product.

216
00:10:36,086 --> 00:10:37,835
Then reach for the matching tool.

217
00:10:37,934 --> 00:10:42,577
Solutions: factor if it's quick,
otherwise use the formula or Desmos.

218
00:10:43,005 --> 00:10:46,343
Vertex, max, or min:
negative b over two a,

219
00:10:46,363 --> 00:10:49,255
vertex form, or click the
top or bottom of the graph.

220
00:10:49,863 --> 00:10:52,220
Number of solutions: the discriminant.

221
00:10:52,541 --> 00:10:56,327
Sum or product: negative
b over a, and c over a.

222
00:10:56,408 --> 00:10:59,730
And before you lock in an
answer, reread the question.

223
00:11:00,480 --> 00:11:02,551
A vertex has two numbers.

224
00:11:02,980 --> 00:11:05,551
Make sure you're giving
the one they asked for.

225
00:11:05,634 --> 00:11:06,634
Recap.

226
00:11:06,991 --> 00:11:09,348
Standard form shows the y intercept.

227
00:11:09,777 --> 00:11:12,599
Factored form shows the
roots, with the signs flipped.

228
00:11:13,241 --> 00:11:16,241
Vertex form shows the
vertex, and the max or min.

229
00:11:17,563 --> 00:11:19,292
The discriminant counts solutions.

230
00:11:19,312 --> 00:11:23,634
And the solutions add to negative
b over a and multiply to c over a.

231
00:11:23,691 --> 00:11:27,599
Every question in this video was written
for this video in the style of the real

232
00:11:27,619 --> 00:11:28,619
test.

233
00:11:28,869 --> 00:11:32,849
For official practice, the College Board's
free Question Bank lets you filter by

234
00:11:32,869 --> 00:11:35,476
domain, skill, and difficulty.

235
00:11:35,552 --> 00:11:37,267
If this helped, subscribe.

236
00:11:37,838 --> 00:11:40,854
Next up is linear functions
and word problems,

237
00:11:40,874 --> 00:11:43,980
including how to read what
the slope actually means.
